  "format": "aerospace_nu_ground_station_text",
  "notes": [
    "`time_stamp_ms` read in milliseconds, from its name and the ground station's clock: over the longest stretch of packets, 22.0 s of the ground station's clock, the board's advances 22.0 s read in milliseconds. The stamps in it keep within 2 s of one gap from the ground station's clock. That is 0.9997 for each second. The band is 0.8 to 1.25 over at least 20 s",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.barometer_pressure` read in atmospheres, from its size and its step: its first value is 0.9707179665565491, a pad's pressure in atmospheres or bars if within 0.4935 to 1.1. A value counts as a whole number within its own rounding as sent. Of its 20 distinct non-zero values, 100.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 101,325. 5.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 100,000",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.barometer_2_pressure` read in atmospheres, from its size and its step: its first value is 0.9706982374191284, a pad's pressure in atmospheres or bars if within 0.4935 to 1.1. A value counts as a whole number within its own rounding as sent. Of its 20 distinct non-zero values, 100.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 101,325. 0.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 100,000",
    "`Ground Station GPS.gs_baro` read in atmospheres, from its size and its step: its first value is 0.9715568714532445, a pad's pressure in atmospheres or bars if within 0.4935 to 1.1. A value counts as a whole number within its own rounding as sent. Of its 12 distinct non-zero values, 100.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 101,325. 0.0% are a whole number of pascals divided by 100,000",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.press_ref` read in atmospheres, from its size and the barometer's: its first value, 0.970724880695343, is 0.001% from `barometer_pressure`'s in the same packet, 0.9707179665565491, read in atmospheres; atmospheres and bars are 1.3% apart",
    "`Position Data.fcb_altitude` read in meters, from the barometer and the coast: from `barometer_pressure`'s first value to its lowest, each within 0.5 s of a sample of the column, the standard atmosphere climbs 178.2 m. The column's climb is 178.1, 1.000 times that. Meters need within 25%. Over the coast, 10 samples across 5.0 s, the column's least-squares parabola slows it 10.09 m/s², 1.029 g read so. An upward coast slows at least 1 g. The band is a factor of 1.8 either way, where feet would read 3.28 times",
    "`Position Data.v_speed` read in meters per second, from the barometer and the coast: over the barometer's ascent, the standard atmosphere climbs 178.2 m. The ascent is the 7.0 s from where its pressure last began to fall to its lowest. The column integrates to 174.5, the speed taken as a straight line between samples up to 1.0 s apart. The climb is 1.021 times that. Meters per second need at least 10 m and within 25%. Over the coast, 11 samples across 5.5 s, the column's least-squares line slows it 10.84 m/s², 1.105 g read so. An upward coast slows at least 1 g. The band is a factor of 1.8 either way, where feet would read 3.28 times",
    "`Position Data.fcb_latitude` and `Position Data.fcb_longitude` read in degrees, from their range and their fractions: 40 fixes, all within ±90° and ±180°, 40 beyond ±π/2 or ±π. 40 of them have a part after the whole degrees of 0.6 or more, where degrees and minutes run together stay under 0.6. Degrees need all within and most of the fixes past both",
    "`Ground Station GPS.gs_lat` and `Ground Station GPS.gs_lon` read in degrees, from their range and their fractions: 11 fixes, all within ±90° and ±180°, 11 beyond ±π/2 or ±π. 11 of them have a part after the whole degrees of 0.6 or more, where degrees and minutes run together stay under 0.6. Degrees need all within and most of the fixes past both",
    "`Orientation.accel_x`, `Orientation.accel_y` and `Orientation.accel_z` read in meters per second squared, from the pad's gravity and the barometer: the three axes' magnitude reads within 10% of 9.806 65 for 15.0 s of the file's time. It reads within 10% of 1 for 0.0 s. A board at rest or under a parachute reads 1 g. Meters per second squared need at least 1 s and twice the other's. From the launch, its specific force along the pad's reading, less 9.806 65, integrates read in m/s² to a climb. At 6 pressures past 10 m of it, the barometer's climb in the standard atmosphere is 1.122 times it, as a median. The band is a factor of 1.8 either way",
    "`Orientation.angle_vertical` read in degrees, from its range and the accelerometer: its values run from 0 to 31.4. The accelerometer reads within 5% of 1 g at 52 samples. At these, the median difference from the angle of the accelerometer's reading from the z axis is 0.02° read in degrees. Read in radians, it is 1221.61°",
    "`Orientation.rot_vel_x`, `Orientation.rot_vel_y` and `Orientation.rot_vel_z` read in radians per second, from the board's turning and its tilt: over 4 stretches of 10 steps at most 0.3 s apart at about 1 g, the accelerometer's reading turns 2.243 rad. The gyroscope turns the board across it 3.077 rad read in radians per second, within a quarter to 4 times. Over 7 windows of at most 2 s in which `angle_vertical` moves at least 10°, it changes 2.482 rad. The gyroscope turns the board across its z axis 3.837 rad read in radians per second and 0.067 rad read in degrees. So degrees per second turn too little for the tilt",
    "`Orientation.magnetic_field_x`, `Orientation.magnetic_field_y` and `Orientation.magnetic_field_z` kept as written, with no quantity for a magnetic field: the record has none, and their names state no unit; their values run from -0.05 to 0.39",
    "`Orientation.roll`, `Orientation.pitch`, `Orientation.yaw`, `Orientation.orientation_rpy[0]`, `Orientation.orientation_rpy[1]` and `Orientation.orientation_rpy[2]` kept as written, with no check of their unit but their range: within ±π they read as radians would, but nothing else in the file checks them; their values run from -0.5489 to 0.5486",
    "`Position Data.temperature` kept as written, in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit alike: its name states no unit, and nothing in the file tells the two apart; its values run from 22.75 to 22.75",
    "`Position Data.gps_alt` kept as written, with no check of its unit but the barometer's: a GPS altitude's rise against the barometer's tells meters from feet, but no second check independent of the barometer is in the file; its values run from 250 to 428.1000061035156",
    "`Position Data.fcb_battery_voltage` kept as written, in a unit nothing in the file checks: its name states no unit, and no check in the file reaches one; its values run from 8.100000381469727 to 8.100000381469727",
    "`Position Data.ground_speed` kept as written, in a unit nothing in the file checks: its name states no unit, and no check in the file reaches one; its values run from 0 to 0",
    "`Position Data.course_over_ground` kept as written, in a unit nothing in the file checks: its name states no unit, and no check in the file reaches one; its values run from 0 to 0",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.ground_elev` kept as written, in a unit nothing in the file checks: its name states no unit, and no check in the file reaches one; its values run from 0 to 0",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.ground_temp` kept as written, in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit alike: its name states no unit, and nothing in the file tells the two apart; its values run from 18 to 18",
    "`Alt Info & Cfg.pitot_ducer_press` kept as written, in a unit nothing in the file checks: its name states no unit, and no check in the file reaches one; its values run from 0 to 0",
    "`Ground Station GPS.gs_alt` kept as written, with no check of its unit but the barometer's: a GPS altitude's rise against the barometer's tells meters from feet, but no second check independent of the barometer is in the file; its values run from 250 to 250",
    "`Ground Station GPS.gs_temp` kept as written, in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit alike: its name states no unit, and nothing in the file tells the two apart; its values run from 31.5 to 31.5",
    "2 packets, the first on line 64, are left out: the ground station marks their `crc` other than `'Good'`, their bytes having failed the radio's checksum",
    "2 lines are the ground station's own messages, not packets, such as \"Switching radio to band 2\" on line 2: skipped",
    "1 value, on line 106, is `None`, `nan`, `inf` or text that isn't a number: it is a gap",
    "1 position of (0, 0), the receiver's mark for no fix, is a gap",
    "the fields `callsign`, `radio_name` hold text, not numbers: they are left out of the channels; `crc` decides which packets are read"
  ],
